WEBVTT

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:02.370
Absolutely not!

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:05.670
Going to a restaurant when you
already get meals from the institution,

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:08.420
is what I call a luxury!

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:14.510
I'm sure you're doing this for Martin,

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:17.640
but why not just leave things to the police?

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:23.390
I'll take care of things by myself this time.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.100
Huh?

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.060
I'll help!

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:35.160
I'll definitely return this favor.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:39.950
I was able to help you
because of Sophie's help.

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:44.000
If you're gonna return the favor,
you should return it to her.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.230
Miss Melia Wild?

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:09.060
I am Pawn, the one who contacted you.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:14.400
Thank you very much
for taking an interest in us.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:18.370
I read the e-mail. Those are pretty good terms.

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:23.410
Well, that's to be expected
since you are trying to head hunt me.

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:28.000
I hope we can go into a little more detail?

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.920
About this El Dorado,
that wants my skills so badly.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:35.010
Yes, of course.

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:38.590
A certain problem has come up though.

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:40.100
What is it?

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.430
I've gotten a little hungry.

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:44.850
Huh?

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.740
Oh, that was bad of me.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:57.650
We'll have to find someone else now.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.490
I-Is there something that you need?!

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:03.870
There is no reason
for you to trouble yourself,

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:06.830
we have enough help on this side!

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:08.750
Master Knight.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:58.650
Our special menu for today!

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:03.990
Missing person cases.

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:08.080
These last two weeks, they've
been happening one after another.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:12.080
They are all in their
late teens or in their twenties.

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:15.330
While Horrors have been
sensed at various locations,

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:17.540
the specifics are still unknown.

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:20.670
One of the missing victims
left a friend an e-mail saying,

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.340
"I'm being scouted by El Dorado."

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.140
Let me see!

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:28.640
Sword!

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:30.930
Don't follow me!

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:35.650
I don't have time to deal
with you this time. Go home!

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:37.810
Give it up.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:41.610
Why?

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:46.870
What is El Dorado?
Why is Sword chasing after it?

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:50.660
I'm sure he'll tell you once he is ready.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:00.630
Whoa.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:06.380
Hey, now. Are you trying to pass
through here without greeting us?!

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:08.220
Haven't seen your face before.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:12.720
Looks like we need to teach you
about the rules around here.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:14.730
Hey.

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:20.230
Yeah, that's right.

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:22.610
He definitely said something like that.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:27.610
"If I go to El Dorado,
I'll be able to live a better life."

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:32.080
Isn't El Dorado the name of some
ancient civilization or something?

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:36.750
The city of gold.
A legend from the Andes region.

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:40.750
Does that have anything
to do with him missing?

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:45.130
That's what I'm looking
into right now. Anything else?

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:47.300
Not really.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:49.180
If I knew something like this would happen,

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:51.680
I should have asked for more details.

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:57.810
Even private detectives are getting involved.
Did he do something bad?

00:05:57.810 --> 00:06:02.860
No, well. We're just following
up on a client's request.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:07.070
I see. Well, the police
are useless around here.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:12.200
The victims were all single
or working away from home.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:14.410
They had few acquaintances,
if any, in the city,

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:17.790
making it difficult for others to notice
when they suddenly go missing.

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:21.380
College student. Programmer.
Neuroscience researcher.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:23.340
Specialist in electronic engineering.

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:25.920
An internet game vlogger.

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:32.510
The only thing in common is that
they are involved with the internet.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:39.060
It's more difficult to find people
<i>not</i> involved with the net these days.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:43.440
That man was the only person
who mentioned the word El Dorado.

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:47.610
The others may not be involved
or they didn't have anyone to tell.

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:50.360
Or they were silenced.

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:52.660
If you get too caught up with this keyword,

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:55.040
you may lose the big picture.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:02.130
Don't worry. I'll do my job properly.

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:15.510
Is El Dorado a place? Or could it
be the name of an organization?

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:20.980
Looking for a person?

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:25.520
People move in and outta here fast.

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:31.110
No one remembers things from three years ago.

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:32.820
On top of that, a kid?

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:37.290
If they're lucky, they're sent to a home.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:41.460
Most of them join a gang or are long dead.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:44.540
Oh, and you said it was a girl?

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:48.210
Then she might be standing
on a street corner somewhere.

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:54.720
Oh, hey! I gave you information
so give me something! Hey!

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:59.930
A new experience in virtual reality!

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:02.440
Easy retina scan access!

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:05.900
ELDO NET is currently open for beta testing!

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:11.150
Oh, I noticed the guy hadn't been
posting lately. He went missing?

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:12.610
Must've ran out of ideas.

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:16.320
Huh? Seriously? Isn't this
getting to be a real problem?

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:18.120
I'm pretty much also
struggling with school credits.

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:19.830
Wish I could just disconnect from it. LOL

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:23.160
Has there been any talk
about it in direct messaging?

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:26.840
100% sure he's pulling a prank for the views!

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:31.590
Speaking of disappearances.
Anyone know where Team Omega went?

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:33.260
Team Omega?

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:36.720
Remember the online game, Dark Strike?

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:38.930
They were always at the top of the rankings,

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:40.890
but they suddenly disappeared.

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:42.930
Bet they got tired of it and quit.

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:47.400
No. No. No. They're all junkies over there.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:50.780
Good riddance. Their chat
messages were always annoying.

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:54.700
All of it were inside jokes
no one else understood.

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:57.620
Stuff like, "Get on the El Dorado bus!"

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.530
El Dorado bus?

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:02.830
They were all hyped up
about it before disappearing.

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:06.460
"If you go to El Dorado,
you'll find happiness." Or something.

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:08.960
Isn't that dangerous? A cult?

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:10.500
Maybe so.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:25.770
Where are you going, Sophie?

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:29.980
Oh, uh! For a walk!

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:33.900
Then why are you trying
to sneak out the back?

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:39.660
Listen, Sophie.

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:44.120
It's too late, after the fact.

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:48.580
You've just been lucky until now.
Do you understand?

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:51.500
But, Sister. I'm not...

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:53.550
I understand how you feel.

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:58.430
But you're still just a child.

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:02.310
I want to protect you until
you become an adult.

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:05.560
Yes...

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:13.150
Please wait a moment.

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:23.540
Thank you for waiting.

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:26.870
I'm sorry for visiting so suddenly.

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:32.040
I am tour coordinator
for educational institutions.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:35.590
An education agent, Pawn.

00:11:03.070 --> 00:11:05.910
Don't move! What are you doing here?!

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:28.680
"Get on the El Dorado bus"...?

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:33.690
Yeah. About ten days ago,
that seven-member team

00:11:33.690 --> 00:11:36.860
suddenly stopped logging in.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:40.950
That's the shop the team
used to meet up offline.

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:43.410
Their leader works part-time there.

00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:46.410
So when they meet, it's usually that shop.

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:52.750
That area is where
Mr. Luke is currently looking.

00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:56.710
I'll contact him!

00:11:58.460 --> 00:12:00.630
I don't know if it'll be much help.

00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:06.640
No, it is. Thanks.

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:09.810
Sorry about earlier.

00:12:09.810 --> 00:12:14.400
I know that you're not a
stranger to El Dorado yourself.

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:18.440
Once I find something out,
I'll definitely tell you.

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:19.690
Thanks!

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:20.900
But!

00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:26.280
Go home for today. Leave the rest to us.

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:27.280
Yeah!

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:36.420
That shop, huh?

00:13:01.610 --> 00:13:03.530
There it is.

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:39.520
They did a pretty good job hiding it...

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:41.690
It's a barrier made by a Horror.

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:55.620
Still breathing.

00:13:55.620 --> 00:13:59.170
Looks like they're all just unconscious.

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:01.420
It's like a storage unit.

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:03.420
Could it be like the last one,

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:06.510
storing them and eating them up one by one?

00:14:06.510 --> 00:14:10.010
Maybe they wanted to
put them "on the bus" instead.

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:13.310
They're sending them out of the city?

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:16.020
Could there be a nest
of Horrors somewhere?

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:17.600
I'll call for back-up.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:20.400
We can't handle of all
these hostages ourselves.

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:24.820
It's me. We found the missing people.

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:29.280
That's right. We don't have enough people.

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:31.990
Send a request for help
to Fei Long and the others.

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:35.700
The number of victims...

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:40.670
The targets for the Horror?

00:14:40.670 --> 00:14:46.170
All the areas you've been
walking around in are there.

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:48.420
This place...

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:52.180
Understood. We'll wait at the site.

00:14:52.180 --> 00:14:53.390
Hey!

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:58.730
Sophie's home is marked on the Horror's map!

00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:03.480
This is an emergency! Sword has--

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:06.780
Sorry. We have an
emergency order here ourselves.

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:08.950
We just got word.

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:14.370
It looks like something
crazy is wandering around.

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:17.450
Please leave the victims to Mr. Fei Long.

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:19.660
Mr. Luke, please go and support Mr. Sword.

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:21.080
Understood.

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:25.630
What the hell is going on?

00:15:36.720 --> 00:15:40.480
Everyone! I have some
wonderful news for you today.

00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:44.770
Next month, everyone
will be going camping!

00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:48.030
What?!

00:15:48.030 --> 00:15:52.070
Camping? Do we have that kind of money?

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:55.620
Children shouldn't worry about such things.

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:58.200
A representative came
today and informed us

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:02.000
about an affordable tour specially
made for institutions like us.

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:05.960
Shouldn't we take this
chance to go out together?

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:07.090
Right!

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:09.590
Hey! Hey! Where are we going camping?

00:16:09.590 --> 00:16:12.050
I heard it was a wonderful place!

00:16:12.050 --> 00:16:14.890
The facility is new, so it's not well-known.

00:16:14.890 --> 00:16:18.470
But I've been told everyone
who went found happiness there!

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:24.190
"If you go to El Dorado,
you'll find happiness." Or something.

00:16:24.190 --> 00:16:28.570
Sister, that affordable tour...

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:30.190
Please wait a moment.

00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:36.120
Yes!

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:38.580
Who is here at a time like this?

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:41.580
You are...

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:44.330
I am sorry for bothering you so late.

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:47.080
The preparations for the tour is complete,

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:49.210
so we've come to pick you up.

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:50.670
What?

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:57.140
Um, it's true I accepted
your offer, but this is sudden.

00:16:57.140 --> 00:16:59.560
Wasn't it supposed to
be two weeks from now?

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:01.930
They often say, "Better now than later."

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:04.100
You are all very lucky.

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:07.400
Now, please grasp for the happiness.

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:11.030
At the city of miracles, El Dorado!

00:17:12.150 --> 00:17:16.410
But we are not prepared
to suddenly leave like this.

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:19.660
Your circumstances do not matter.

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:26.460
Things have changed,
we must leave the city immediately.

00:17:26.460 --> 00:17:28.790
You are all third-rate products.

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:34.630
You cannot support El Dorado,
but you will be useful as food.

00:17:34.630 --> 00:17:40.300
I cannot appear before
the king empty-handed!

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:41.760
Sister!

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:45.730
Sophie! Take everyone to Mr. Brooks!

00:17:45.730 --> 00:17:47.480
Tell them to call the police!

00:17:47.480 --> 00:17:50.360
No! He might be a Horror!

00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:52.690
--You have to come with us, Sister!
--Hurry!

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:01.910
I won't let you escape!

00:18:10.420 --> 00:18:15.010
I won't let you lay a finger on my children!

00:18:25.770 --> 00:18:28.560
Teacher! Mr. Brooks!

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:31.610
Teacher! Teacher!

00:18:37.240 --> 00:18:39.910
What's going on, at a time like this?!

00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:42.240
A crazy person is at the home!

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:45.040
Please call the police! Please!

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:46.910
--Sophie!
--Sophie!

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:04.680
Calm down! Calm down!

00:19:08.640 --> 00:19:09.480
Hi, this is the diner!

00:19:09.480 --> 00:19:11.060
Please call Sword!

00:19:11.060 --> 00:19:12.440
Hurry!

00:19:54.270 --> 00:19:56.860
You can't!

00:20:14.540 --> 00:20:16.880
Don't get in my way.

00:20:41.070 --> 00:20:45.240
Wait. What do you plan to do to Sophie...?

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:18.230
Run... away...

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:37.460
Sophia Hennes. I have been looking for you.

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:44.340
My master, the King of
El Dorado, summons you.

00:21:52.970 --> 00:21:54.980
You!

00:21:57.480 --> 00:21:59.480
Garo, huh?

00:22:10.570 --> 00:22:14.910
You finally appeared before me.

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:19.500
Dark Knight!
